# Executive Summary

TechGrowth Solutions closed 2024 with an outstanding fourth quarter, capping
what has been an exceptional year for the business. Revenue reached
**$187.3M**, up **23.8%** year over year, while EBITDA rose to **$42.1M**, a
**22.5%** margin. Earnings per share came in at **$1.47**, beating consensus
estimates by $0.12, and free cash flow grew 31% year over year to $38.4M.

Every headline metric this quarter exceeded the ranges the company gave at
the start of Q4, and the momentum was broad-based: revenue growth
accelerated for the fourth consecutive quarter, net revenue retention climbed
to 126%, and the active customer base grew 40% year over year to nearly
4,000 accounts. The remainder of this report walks through the drivers of
that performance, the state of the balance sheet, the guidance the company
is issuing for 2025, and the risks the board and management team are
actively managing.

::: success
**Q4 2024 at a glance**
- Revenue: $187.3M (+23.8% year over year)
- EBITDA: $42.1M (22.5% margin)
- EPS: $1.47 (beat consensus by $0.12)
- Free cash flow: $38.4M (+31% year over year)
- Net revenue retention: 126%
:::

# Revenue Performance

## Quarterly Trend

Revenue has now grown for eight consecutive quarters, and — notably — the
rate of growth itself has been accelerating rather than merely holding
steady. Q4 2024's 23.8% year-over-year growth is the highest of the year,
building on a base that was already growing at a low-20s clip twelve months
earlier. Management attributes the acceleration to the maturation of the
software segment and to the international expansion that began in early
2024.

