## Geographic Distribution

North America continues to anchor the business, but Asia-Pacific is the
fastest-growing region on a percentage basis, expanding 28.6% year over
year as the company's regional go-to-market investments begin to pay off.

| Region | Q4 2024 | Q4 2023 | Growth | % of Total |
|--------|---------|---------|--------|------------|
| North America | $112.4M | $89.2M | +26.0% | 60% |
| Europe | $48.7M | $41.8M | +16.5% | 26% |
| Asia-Pacific | $18.9M | $14.7M | +28.6% | 10% |
| Other | $7.3M | $5.5M | +32.7% | 4% |

"Other" primarily reflects early revenue from Latin America and other
emerging markets that the company began serving directly in 2024.

# Profitability

EBITDA reached $42.1M in Q4 2024, a 22.5% margin that represents 130 basis
points of expansion over the prior-year quarter. The improvement reflects
genuine operating leverage rather than one-time cost cuts: as the software
segment scales, incremental revenue carries a materially higher margin than
the company's historical average, and cost discipline in go-to-market
spending has kept operating expenses growing more slowly than revenue.

