The company's 22.5% EBITDA margin compares favorably to the industry
average for its peer group, and management believes there is further room
for expansion as the software mix continues to grow relative to
professional services.

# Cash Flow & Balance Sheet

Operating cash flow of $41.2M and free cash flow of $38.4M both grew faster
than revenue this quarter, reflecting strong collections and disciplined
capital expenditure. The balance sheet strengthened accordingly: cash and
equivalents grew to $95.7M while total debt was reduced by 23.1%, leaving
the company in a net cash position of $70.7M — an improvement of $26.5M
versus the prior-year quarter.

| Metric | Q4 2024 | Q4 2023 | Change |
|--------|---------|---------|--------|
| Operating Cash Flow | $41.2M | $31.8M | +29.6% |
| Free Cash Flow | $38.4M | $29.3M | +31.1% |
| Cash & Equivalents | $95.7M | $73.2M | +30.7% |
| Total Debt | $25.0M | $32.5M | -23.1% |

This financial flexibility gives the company room to fund its 2025 growth
initiatives largely from internally generated cash, without needing to draw
on external financing or dilute shareholders.

## Customer Metrics

The customer base grew 40% year over year to 3,985 active accounts, and
net revenue retention climbed to 126% — meaning that, on average, existing
customers are expanding their spend well beyond what churn takes away.
That combination of new-logo growth and expansion revenue from the existing
base is the clearest evidence of durable, compounding demand for the
platform.

